WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.390
Let's make Leaf-rubbing discoveries.

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:07.359
Reveal veins and edges by rubbing a wax crayon sideways over paper with a

3
00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:08.015
leaf underneath.

4
00:00:08.395 --> 00:00:10.475
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:10.855 --> 00:00:13.585
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:13.965 --> 00:00:16.210
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.915
An adult checks the plant pieces and prepares crayons.

8
00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:24.040
Use leaves that lie flat, with no thorns or irritating sap.

9
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.690
Step 1.

10
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.805
Feel the leaf pattern.

11
00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:33.000
Set one leaf on the table with its bumpy underside facing up.

12
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.380
Gently feel the raised veins with a fingertip.

13
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.270
Choose a leaf that lies mostly flat.

14
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.030
Grown-up help.

15
00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.430
Check the leaves before handling.

16
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:46.013
Step 2.

17
00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:48.033
Hide it under paper.

18
00:00:48.413 --> 00:00:50.918
Lay a sheet of thin paper over the leaf.

19
00:00:51.298 --> 00:00:55.242
Put a small piece of paper tape at two corners of the sheet to

20
00:00:55.242 --> 00:00:56.368
keep it from sliding.

21
00:00:56.748 --> 00:00:58.128
Grown-up help.

22
00:00:58.508 --> 00:01:00.693
Help hold or tape the paper.

23
00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.512
Step 3.

24
00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:05.797
Turn the crayon sideways.

25
00:01:06.177 --> 00:01:08.827
Lay the broad side of the crayon on the paper.

26
00:01:09.207 --> 00:01:11.572
Hold the paper with the other hand.

27
00:01:11.952 --> 00:01:15.102
Make two gentle practice strokes beside the leaf.

28
00:01:15.482 --> 00:01:16.862
Grown-up help.

29
00:01:17.242 --> 00:01:19.117
Prepare the unwrapped crayon.

30
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.650
Step 4.

31
00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.480
Rub and reveal.

32
00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.520
Move the crayon back and forth across the hidden leaf with light pressure.

33
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.135
Start at one edge and work across.

34
00:01:30.515 --> 00:01:34.380
Stop when the veins appear; pressing harder can hide the pattern.

35
00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:37.008
Step 5.

36
00:01:37.388 --> 00:01:39.048
Make a leafy page.

37
00:01:39.428 --> 00:01:42.268
Lift the paper and move the leaf to a new spot.

38
00:01:42.648 --> 00:01:45.473
Try another crayon colour or a different leaf.

39
00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:50.258
Leave a little space around each print, then sign or name the artwork.

40
00:01:50.638 --> 00:01:52.018
Grown-up help.

41
00:01:52.398 --> 00:01:54.463
Remove tape gently at the end.

42
00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.915
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

43
00:01:59.295 --> 00:02:02.845
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

44
00:02:03.225 --> 00:02:05.245
Your creation can look different.

45
00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.735
Reuse crayons and sort paper.

46
00:02:08.115 --> 00:02:11.695
Return or dispose of untreated leaves appropriately.

47
00:02:12.075 --> 00:02:15.200
Keep the dry rubbing in a folder or display it indoors.

48
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.570
Well done.

49
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.380
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

